                        




SCP-XXXX Pre-Containment



Item #:  SCP-5083

Object Class:  Safe

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5083 is held in a standard humanoid containment cell in Site-107's anomalous humanoid wing, and is to be fed a serving of 10kg of hay daily. SCP-5083-1 instances are to be removed from SCP-5083's cell when they are produced.

Description:  SCP-5083 is a humanoid with a head resembling that of a oryctolagus cuniculus(European rabbit). SCP-5083 is 1.9 is attached to SCP-5083's right calf.

SCP-5083 has the ability to dispense small plastic containers in the shape of eggs from its rectum, referred to as SCP-5083-1. SCP-5083-1 instances are 1.5cm in height. When dispensing instances of SCP-5083-1, SCP-5083 assumes a squatting position and makes strenuous vocalizations indicative of intestinal/rectal distress. SCP-5083 dispenses one SCP-5083-1 instance every hour.

When SCP-5083-1 is opened, a small, non-anomalous piece of candy can be found inside. Candy that has been recorded to appear inside SCP-5083-1 include an egg-shaped lollipop, a chocolate egg, a pack of gummy snacks that are rabbit-shaped, and a pack of jelly beans.

On Easter Sunday at 9 AM, SCP-5083 will dispense a total of 20 SCP-5083-1 instances all at once. SCP-5083 expresses heightened discomfort compared to its normal dispensing process during this period.

SCP-5083 was discovered when witnesses reported a man in a rabbit costume  near the edge of a bridge. SCP-5083 refused to tell researchers why it was near a bridge when contained.

Addendum-5083-01 - Interview Log:  The following interview was conducted by Dr. Calvin.



BEGIN LOG 

Dr. Calvin:  Good afternoon, SCP-5083.

SCP-5083:  Wassup.

Dr. Calvin:  I'm going to ask you a few questions, if that's okay.

SCP-5083:  Yeah, sure. Got nothing better to do.

Dr. Calvin:  Okay then. First off I want to know why dispensing-

SCP-5083:  Wait hold on.

SCP-5083 stands up and goes to the corner of his cell. He squats down and starts to groan and curse constantly. He lets out one final scream until an instance of SCP-5083-1 drops out of his rectum.



SCP-5083:  Jesus Christ. Aight now I can talk. What's the question?

SCP-5083 sits back down.

Dr. Calvin:  Why does dispensing SCP-5083-1 bring you so much pain?

SCP-5083:  You're talking about the eggs, right?

Dr. Calvin:  Yes, I mean you just di-

SCP-5083:  Yeah I know. When working on me, the oh-so-wonderful and the oh-so-flawless Dr. Wondertainment was very insistent with the idea of me  the eggs. So what did they think was the best way to do that? They thought that producing them inside of my digestive system was the way to go. I dunno what goes through Dr. Wondertainment's mind sometimes when they're making the stuff they do.

Dr. Calvin:  I see. Can you produce SCP-5083-1 instances whenever you want?

SCP-5083:  Nah. You probably know by now that Dr. Wondertainment isn't the best at producing adequate personalities to accompany their humanoid toys, so they just strip us of some of our free will. If I had the choice to do my little party trick whenever I wanted, I probably wouldn't do it at all. I'm sure Mr. Laugh would say the same. I feel for that guy.

Dr. Calvin:  Alright, next question. Why were you near a bridge when the Foundation contained you?

There is a moment of silence.

SCP-5083:  You know, if I'm being honest with you, I wouldn't mind being an egg-dispensing Easter bunny if it weren't for my abysmal design. I'm not the biggest fan of children, but it sucks to see parents covering their children's eyes when they see me, you know? I was built to bring joy to people, right? If so, why was I made so wrong?

Dr. Calvin:  You didn't answer the question.

There is another moment of silence.

SCP-5083:  Okay, I think I'm done.

SCP-5083 sniffles.

SCP-5083:  If this is all we're doing, just asking questions that lead to nowhere, I don't want to do it.

Dr. Calvin:  SCP-5083, I-

SCP-5083:  No, I don't wanna do this anymore. I'm done.

SCP-5083 goes to the corner of his cell, curls up, and cries continuously. SCP-5083 refuses to communicate any further.

END LOG 
